# ProjectHub API requests. In Rider: start the API (Run or Debug, "http" profile), then click the green
# arrow next to any request. Each "###" starts a new request. Expected status codes are in the titles.
# Since Topic 10 the data lives in SQL Server: it SURVIVES restarts, and new ids are not predictable
# (identity gaps, Topic 8). So the create request saves the new id in a variable ({{projectId}}) for the next ones.
# Run the requests from "create" to "delete again" in order. Reset everything: dotnet ef database drop --force,
# then dotnet ef database update (see lesson 10).

@host = http://localhost:5064

### 200: list of project summaries
GET {{host}}/api/projects

### 200: one project with its tasks (status as text: "Todo", "InProgress", "Done")
GET {{host}}/api/projects/1

### 404: no such project
GET {{host}}/api/projects/999

### 404 with an empty body: "abc" doesn't match the {id:int} route constraint, so no action is found
GET {{host}}/api/projects/abc

### 201 Created + Location header: create a project (saves its id as {{projectId}})
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Docs portal",
  "description": "Public API docs"
}

> {%
    // Response handler (JavaScript, runs in Rider after the response): remember the generated id.
    client.global.set("projectId", response.body.id);
%}

### 409 Conflict: the name is taken (case-insensitive)
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "WEBSITE REDESIGN"
}

### 400: our business rule (empty after trimming)
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   "
}

### 400: automatic model validation by [ApiController] ("name" is a non-nullable string, so it is required)
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "no name"
}

### 200: update the project created above
PUT {{host}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Docs portal v2",
  "description": "Renamed"
}

### 409: it may not take ANOTHER project's name
PUT {{host}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mobile app"
}

### 404: update a project that doesn't exist
PUT {{host}}/api/projects/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost"
}

### 201 Created: add a task to it, with an optional due date (UTC: the "Z" at the end)
POST {{host}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Write getting started",
  "dueDate": "2026-11-01T17:00:00Z"
}

### 400 (Topic 10): description longer than 1000 characters (the column is NVARCHAR(1000))
POST {{host}}/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Too long",
  "description": ""
}

### 404: add a task to a project that doesn't exist
POST {{host}}/api/projects/999/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Ghost task"
}

### 204 No Content: delete it (its tasks go too: ON DELETE CASCADE)
DELETE {{host}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}

### 404: delete it again
DELETE {{host}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}

### Topic 7 lab: DI lifetimes. Send it TWICE and compare the ids (singleton / scoped / transient)
GET {{host}}/api/labs/lifetimes

### Topic 7: look at the X-Response-Time-Ms response header (added by RequestTimingMiddleware)
GET {{host}}/api/projects
